Implemented [IRWB-022-D](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-D--checked-lowering-of-tix-to-cuda-on-the-gpu-machine/index.md). `src/tensor/index.ts` exports `cudaSource`, `runTixCuda`, and `checkLowering`. The backend emits one kernel per statement from the current Tix IR, including after `inline` and `split-sum`.

**Correctness:** All six corpus programs passed the sampled contract against the original f64 reference. Conv2d used the largest fraction of the error allowance: **24.67%**. The same contract rejected a compiled mutant that dropped part of a reduction tail.

**Validation:** `npm run build` succeeded. `node --test tests/tensor/*.test.mjs` passed **32/32**, including 11 live GB10 tests. All six requested full-size GPU and interpreter timings are in the [measurement report](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-D--checked-lowering-of-tix-to-cuda-on-the-gpu-machine/reference/02-gb10-corpus-measurements-and-validation.md).

**Framework changes: none.** `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts` uses the existing asynchronous batch and verdict-replay interfaces. `tools/cuda-remote.mjs` now isolates concurrent runs, publishes compiled executables atomically under a build lock, and reports the compiler version used in its cache key.

**Deviations from the [revised design](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-D--checked-lowering-of-tix-to-cuda-on-the-gpu-machine/design-doc/01-a-checked-tix-to-cuda-lowering-on-gb10.md):** kernels receive the full function shape struct rather than individually selected dimensions; device loads check bounds; every nonempty run warms the kernel chain before event timing. The numerical budget was unchanged.

**Commits:** `f85f8bc` design and probe; `e82d3a7` review revision; `79c782b` emitter and runner; `243da40` checked lowering and tests; `b7e6b2b` measurements and report. Worktree clean; nothing pushed.
